.TH "RECORD\-STATUS\.SH" "" "June 2026" ""
.SH "NAME"
\fBrecord\-status\.sh\fR
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBrecord\-status\.sh\fR
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fBrecord\-status\.sh\fR reports the status of a running RECORD workflow by printing a full process listing for every process in the workflow's process tree\. It sources \fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR and uses \fBpidtree\fR to enumerate all child processes of the recorded PID, then runs \fBps \-f\fR on each one\.
.P
If \fBRECORD_START_PROGRAM\fR is running (the PID file exists and \fB/proc/<pid>\fR is present), one \fBps\fR output line is printed per process in the tree, in the format produced by \fBps \-\-no\-headers \-f\fR\.
.P
If the program is not running, a timestamped message is written to standard error, any stale PID file is removed, and the script exits with status \-1\.
.SH "OPTIONS"
This script accepts no options or arguments\. All configuration is supplied via environment variables inherited from \fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR\.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
Returns 0 if \fBRECORD_START_PROGRAM\fR is running and \fBps\fR output is produced successfully\.
.P
Returns \-1 (typically 255) if \fBRECORD_START_PROGRAM\fR is not running\.
.P
Returns non\-zero if \fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR validation fails at source time (see \fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR documentation)\.
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
.TP
\fBRECORD_START_PROGRAM\fR
The name of the workflow program being monitored\. Set and validated by \fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR at source time\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_DBTYPE\fR
Used by \fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR to construct the PID file path\.
.TP
\fBRECORD_PID_FILE\fR
Path to the PID file, exported by \fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR as \fB/tmp/record\.$USER\.$RECORD_DBTYPE\.$RECORD_START_PROGRAM\.pid\fR\. Removed if found stale (program not running)\.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
Check the status of a running workflow:
.IP "" 4
.nf
export RECORD_START_PROGRAM=my_sim
export RECORD_DBTYPE=sqlite3
record\-status\.sh
.fi
.IP "" 0
.P
Use in a polling loop:
.IP "" 4
.nf
while record\-status\.sh 2>/dev/null; do
    sleep 30
done
echo "Workflow finished\."
.fi
.IP "" 0
.SH "FILES"
.TP
\fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR
Common library sourced at startup\. Must be present in the working directory or on \fBPATH\fR\.
.TP
\fB/tmp/record\.<USER>\.<RECORD_DBTYPE>\.<RECORD_START_PROGRAM>\.pid\fR
PID file identifying the running workflow process\. Removed if the recorded process is no longer alive\.
